    "reconstructionNotes": "RCE monument 504667 and venue architecture page: 1884 Salm horse-tram house with deep stable/forge parent, narrow ENE entrance on Amstelveenseweg. Current facade photo shows red-brick triangular gable, three central upper windows, two carved side rosette fields, ogee flank-window ornaments and pale carved timber windboards. No neighboring tram-remise courts or parents included."
